 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.4.0] - 2026-11-07
+
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates `input` against each tool's declared `inputSchema` before calling the executor. Required fields, declared property types, and enum values are enforced; a failing call returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator can feed the rejection back to the model as a `tool_result` and the model can retry within the existing `maxToolRounds` budget. Extra properties pass through to the executor unchanged, and `additionalProperties: false` is never injected.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Migration note**: an executor that previously hand-validated its input (casting, checking required fields, returning an error message for missing or wrong-typed values) now only receives input that the declared `inputSchema` already accepts. A tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message will no longer see that input; the registry rejects it first.
+
